From: cube oakley <cube-oakley@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 09:50:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] trusty: bind each nop thread to its CPU again when it
 comes back online

Taking a CPU offline parks its trusty-nop thread after the scheduler has
stopped accepting tasks there, so balance_push moves the thread away and
its binding is lost. kthread_unpark() restores the binding only for
KTHREAD_IS_PER_CPU threads (smpboot's), not for kthread_create_on_cpu()
ones. Back online, the CPU's doorbell then woke a thread on another CPU
("trusty-nop-4 ran on wrong cpu, 1"), and a Trusty thread pinned to the
CPU never ran: Goodix's fingerprint app pins itself to CPU 4, and the
Pixel 7 Pro takes CPUs 4-7 offline while the screen is dark.

---
 trusty/trusty.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/trusty/trusty.c b/trusty/trusty.c
--- a/trusty/trusty.c
+++ b/trusty/trusty.c
@@ -1006,6 +1006,14 @@
 
 	s = container_of(node, struct trusty_state, cpuhp_node);
 	tw = this_cpu_ptr(s->nop_works);
+	/*
+	 * kthread_create_on_cpu() does not make the thread KTHREAD_IS_PER_CPU
+	 * (only smpboot threads are), so kthread_unpark() does not bind it
+	 * again, and once this CPU has been offline the thread runs elsewhere.
+	 * Its nops then enter Trusty on the wrong CPU, and a Trusty thread
+	 * pinned to this one never runs.
+	 */
+	set_cpus_allowed_ptr(tw->nop_thread, cpumask_of(cpu));
 	kthread_unpark(tw->nop_thread);
 
 	dev_dbg(s->dev, "cpu %d up\n", cpu);
